{"id":"1a09513a24ab7975d29944f55d2236dc050da94f","axis":"silent","repo":"openvinotoolkit/openvino","sha":"1a09513a24ab7975d29944f55d2236dc050da94f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/articles_en/documentation/openvino-extensibility/openvino-plugin-library/compiled-model.rst","lines":["@@ -78,6 +78,29 @@ to import a backend specific graph later in the ``Plugin::import_model`` method:","    :language: cpp","    :fragment: [compiled_model:export_model]"," ","+By default, the Template plugin exports an HSM blob: a container of sections. The export stream must be","+seekable. The blob has these sections:","+","+* model id and runtime requirements","+* compiled options: the values of the properties listed by ``ov::internal::caching_properties`` and","+  ``ov::weights_path``, if it is set","+* model structure (XML) and weights","+* blob info, which tells if the weights are stored in the blob","+","+The plugin adds the sections with a handler that implements ``ov::runtime::hsm::ISectionWriterHandler``.","+Small sections are kept in memory. The model structure and the weights are written to the stream","+while the model is serialized, so the plugin does not make a second copy of them.","+","+.. doxygensnippet:: src/plugins/template/src/hsm_writer_handler.cpp","+   :language: cpp","+   :fragment: [hsm_writer_handler:handle_section]","+","+When the model is compiled with ``ov::cache_mode(ov::CacheMode::OPTIMIZE_SIZE)``, the weights section","+is not written. On import, the weights are restored from ``ov::weights_path``.","+","+To write the legacy layout instead, set ``ov::template_plugin::export_hsm_format`` to ``false``.","+This is a transition switch and is removed together with the legacy format.","+"," create_sync_infer_request()"," +++++++++++++++++++++++++++"," ","@@ -151,4 +174,3 @@ The methods returns the runtime model with backend specific information.","    :fragment: [compiled_model:get_runtime_model]"," "," The next step in plugin library implementation is the :doc:`Synchronous Inference Request <synch-inference-request>` class.","-"],"additions":23,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/articles_en/documentation/openvino-extensibility/openvino-plugin-library/plugin.rst","lines":["@@ -172,6 +172,10 @@ Returns a current value for a specified property key:"," The function is implemented with the ``Configuration::Get`` method, which wraps an actual configuration"," key value to the ov::Any and returns it."," ","+The ``ov::internal::caching_properties`` property lists the properties that affect the compiled model,","+so a model compiled with different values of them is not the same model. The Template plugin returns the","+device architecture, the performance mode, the execution mode and the inference precision.","+"," .. note::"," ","    The function must throw an exception if it receives an unsupported configuration key.","@@ -200,6 +204,25 @@ For example, the export information may include:","    :language: cpp","    :fragment: [plugin:import_model_with_remote]"," ","+For an HSM blob, the Template plugin reads the sections with ``ov::runtime::hsm::Reader``.","+The import works in these steps:","+","+* The model structure and the blob info sections are mandatory.","+* The blob is rejected if its runtime requirements are not supported by the plugin.","+* The compiled options are restored into the plugin configuration. Properties passed to","+  ``import_model`` have a higher priority.","+* The weights are taken from the blob. If the blob has no weights section (for example, it was exported","+  with ``ov::cache_mode(ov::CacheMode::OPTIMIZE_SIZE)``), they are read from ``ov::weights_path``,","+  or from the path stored in the compiled options.","+* Sections that the plugin does not know are skipped, so blobs written by a newer format minor version","+  still import.","+","+If the stream is not an HSM blob, the plugin reads it as the legacy format.","+","+.. doxygensnippet:: src/plugins/template/src/plugin.cpp","+   :language: cpp","+   :fragment: [plugin:read_hsm_blob]","+"," "," create_context()"," ++++++++++++++++","@@ -231,4 +254,3 @@ OpenVINO plugin library must export only one function creating a plugin instance"," "," "," Next step in a plugin library implementation is the :doc:`CompiledModel <compiled-model>` class.","-"],"additions":23,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/inference/src/dev/hsm_reader.cpp","lines":["@@ -80,9 +80,8 @@ bool read_manifest(std::istream& stream,"," }"," "," bool has_container_size_bytes(std::istream& stream, std::streampos start, const Header& header) {","-    stream.seekg(start);","-    stream.ignore(static_cast<std::streamsize>(header.container_size));","-    return stream.gcount() == static_cast<std::streamsize>(header.container_size);","+    stream.seekg(start + static_cast<std::streamoff>(header.container_size - 1));","+    return stream.peek() != std::istream::traits_type::eof();"," }"," "," // 32-bit size_t can't represent every SizeType value - reject oversized sections before they're constructed."],"additions":2,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/inference/tests/unit/hsm_deferred_writer.cpp","lines":["@@ -945,7 +945,7 @@ TEST(HsmDeferredWriterTest, section_encoder_avoids_materializing_a_view_for_a_tr","     public:","         explicit ValueEncoder(int value) : m_value(value) {}","         void encode(const hsm::SectionSink& sink) const override {","-            sink({reinterpret_cast<const std::byte*>(&m_value), sizeof(m_value)});","+            sink(ov::util::as_memory_view(m_value));","         }"," ","     private:","@@ -1044,7 +1044,7 @@ TEST(HsmDeferredWriterTest, handler_forwards_to_a_named_member_function_instead_"," ","     private:","         void write_options(const hsm::SectionSink& sink) const {","-            sink({reinterpret_cast<const std::byte*>(&m_options), sizeof(m_options)});","+            sink(ov::util::as_memory_view(m_options));","         }"," ","         CompiledOptions m_options;"],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/inference/tests/unit/hsm_format.cpp","lines":["@@ -591,7 +591,7 @@ TEST(IHsmSectionExtensionTest, recognizes_own_device_and_tag) {"," ","     const std::byte payload[4] = {};","     RecordingExtension extension;","-    EXPECT_TRUE(extension.read_section(entry, ov::util::MemoryView{payload, 4}));","+    EXPECT_TRUE(extension.read_section(entry, ov::util::as_memory_view(payload)));","     EXPECT_EQ(extension.last_section_size, 4u);"," }"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/inference/tests/unit/hsm_reader.cpp","lines":["@@ -230,7 +230,7 @@ TEST(ISectionReaderHandlerTest, recognizes_own_device_and_tag) {","     entry.size = 4;"," ","     const std::byte payload[4] = {};","-    const hsm::Section section(entry, ov::util::MemoryView{payload, 4});","+    const hsm::Section section(entry, ov::util::as_memory_view(payload));","     RecordingHandler handler(fake_device_id, /*tag_id=*/42);","     EXPECT_TRUE(handler.handle_section(entry, section));","     EXPECT_EQ(handler.last_payload.size(), 4u);"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/plugins/template/include/template/properties.hpp","lines":["@@ -27,5 +27,11 @@ static constexpr Property<bool, PropertyMutability::RW> disable_transformations{"," "," // ! [properties:public_header]"," ","+/**","+ * @brief Selects the export_model() blob format: true = HSM container (default), false = legacy layout.","+ * @note Transition/test-only switch; removed together with the legacy format.","+ */","+static constexpr Property<bool, PropertyMutability::RW> export_hsm_format{\"TEMPLATE_EXPORT_HSM_FORMAT\"};","+"," }  // namespace template_plugin"," }  // namespace ov"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/plugins/template/src/CMakeLists.txt","lines":["@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@ set(SOURCES","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/async_infer_request.cpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/compiled_model.cpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/config.cpp","+    ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/hsm_reader_handler.cpp","+    ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/hsm_writer_handler.cpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/plugin.cpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/remote_context.cpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/sync_infer_request.cpp","@@ -18,6 +20,9 @@ set(HEADERS","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/attach_cache_manager_to_paged_attention.hpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/compiled_model.hpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/config.hpp","+    ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/hsm_common.hpp","+    ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/hsm_reader_handler.hpp","+    ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/hsm_writer_handler.hpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/itt.hpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/plugin.hpp","     ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/remote_context.hpp"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/plugins/template/src/compiled_model.cpp","lines":["@@ -7,10 +7,13 @@"," #include <memory>"," "," #include \"async_infer_request.hpp\"","+#include \"hsm_writer_handler.hpp\""," #include \"itt.hpp\""," #include \"openvino/op/util/op_types.hpp\""," #include \"openvino/pass/serialize.hpp\""," #include \"openvino/runtime/exec_model_info.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_deferred_writer.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/internal_properties.hpp\""," #include \"openvino/runtime/properties.hpp\""," #include \"perf_counter.hpp\""," #include \"plugin.hpp\"","@@ -154,6 +157,8 @@ ov::Any ov::template_plugin::CompiledModel::get_property(const std::string& name","     } else if (ov::runtime_requirements == name) {","         // A real plugin would encode compilation capabilities.","         return std::string(get_template_plugin()->get_runtime_requirements());","+    } else if (ov::internal::caching_properties == name || ov::device::architecture == name) {","+        return get_plugin()->get_property(name, {});","     } else if (ov::supported_properties == name) {","         auto ro_properties = default_ro_properties();","         auto rw_properties = default_rw_properties();","@@ -173,21 +178,35 @@ ov::Any ov::template_plugin::CompiledModel::get_property(const std::string& name"," void ov::template_plugin::CompiledModel::export_model(std::ostream& model_stream) const {","     OV_ITT_SCOPED_TASK(itt::domains::TemplatePlugin, \"CompiledModel::export_model\");"," ","-    std::stringstream xmlFile, binFile;","-    ov::pass::Serialize serializer(xmlFile, binFile);","-    serializer.run_on_model(m_model);","-","-    auto m_constants = binFile.str();","-    auto m_model = xmlFile.str();","-","-    auto dataSize = static_cast<std::uint64_t>(m_model.size());","-    model_stream.write(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&dataSize), sizeof(dataSize));","-    model_stream.write(m_model.c_str(), dataSize);","-","-    if (m_cfg.cache_mode == CacheMode::OPTIMIZE_SPEED) {","-        dataSize = static_cast<std::uint64_t>(m_constants.size());","+    if (m_cfg.export_hsm_format) {","+        ov::AnyMap cache_options;","+        const auto caching_properties = get_property(ov::internal::caching_properties.name());","+        for (const auto& name : caching_properties.as<decltype(ov::internal::caching_properties)::value_type>()) {","+            cache_options.emplace(name, get_property(name));","+        }","+        HsmWriterHandler handler{m_model, m_cfg, cache_options, get_template_plugin()->get_runtime_requirements()};","+        auto writer = ov::runtime::hsm::DeferredWriter::open(model_stream);","+        OPENVINO_ASSERT(writer, \"TEMPLATE: cannot open HSM writer, the export stream must be seekable\");","+        writer->add_sections({&handler});","+        const auto error = writer->finalize();","+        OPENVINO_ASSERT(!error, \"TEMPLATE: HSM export failed: \", error.message());","+    } else {","+        std::stringstream xmlFile, binFile;","+        ov::pass::Serialize serializer(xmlFile, binFile);","+        serializer.run_on_model(m_model);","+","+        auto m_constants = binFile.str();","+        auto m_model = xmlFile.str();","+","+        auto dataSize = static_cast<std::uint64_t>(m_model.size());","         model_stream.write(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&dataSize), sizeof(dataSize));","-        model_stream.write(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&m_constants[0]), dataSize);","+        model_stream.write(m_model.c_str(), dataSize);","+","+        if (m_cfg.cache_mode == CacheMode::OPTIMIZE_SPEED) {","+            dataSize = static_cast<std::uint64_t>(m_constants.size());","+            model_stream.write(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&dataSize), sizeof(dataSize));","+            model_stream.write(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&m_constants[0]), dataSize);","+        }","     }"," }"," // ! [compiled_model:export_model]"],"additions":33,"deletions":14,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/plugins/template/src/config.cpp","lines":["@@ -126,6 +126,8 @@ Configuration::Configuration(const ov::AnyMap& config, const Configuration& defa","             }","         } else if (ov::cache_mode == key) {","             cache_mode = value.as<CacheMode>();","+        } else if (ov::template_plugin::export_hsm_format == key) {","+            export_hsm_format = value.as<bool>();","         } else if (throwOnUnsupported) {","             OPENVINO_THROW(\"Property was not found: \", key);","         }","@@ -175,6 +177,8 @@ ov::Any Configuration::Get(const std::string& name) const {","         return cache_mode;","     } else if (name == ov::internal::cache_header_alignment) {","         return 4096;  // page size in bytes","+    } else if (name == ov::template_plugin::export_hsm_format || name == ov::internal::emit_hsm_format) {","+        return export_hsm_format;","     } else {","         OPENVINO_THROW(\"Property was not found: \", name);","     }"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/plugins/template/src/config.hpp","lines":["@@ -57,6 +57,8 @@ struct Configuration {","     std::filesystem::path weights_path{};","     AnyMap compiled_model_runtime_properties{};","     CacheMode cache_mode{CacheMode::OPTIMIZE_SPEED};","+    // Transition switch: false selects the legacy blob layout; removed together with it.","+    bool export_hsm_format = true;"," };"," // ! [configuration:header]"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/plugins/template/src/hsm_common.hpp","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@","+// Copyright (C) 2018-2026 Intel Corporation","+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+//","+","+// Wire contract of the TEMPLATE HSM blob (device id, section ids, BlobInfo), shared by HsmReaderHandler and","+// HsmWriterHandler. Keep it free of reader and writer code - the two handlers must stay independent.","+// `hsm` is this plugin's own namespace; the runtime API is spelled runtime::hsm.","+","+#pragma once","+","+#include <cstdint>","+","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_format.hpp\"","+","+namespace ov::template_plugin {","+namespace hsm {","+","+// Placeholder until the HSM device catalog gives TEMPLATE its own id (private range starts at 0x80).","+inline constexpr runtime::hsm::DeviceId device_id = runtime::hsm::private_device_id_range_start;","+struct SectionId {","+    runtime::hsm::DeviceId device;","+    runtime::hsm::SectionTag tag;","+};","+","+constexpr uint32_t section_key(runtime::hsm::DeviceId device, runtime::hsm::SectionTag tag) noexcept {","+    return (static_cast<uint32_t>(device) << 24) | (static_cast<uint32_t>(tag.value[0]) << 16) |","+           (static_cast<uint32_t>(tag.value[1]) << 8) | static_cast<uint32_t>(tag.value[2]);","+}","+","+constexpr uint32_t section_key(const SectionId& id) noexcept {","+    return section_key(id.device, id.tag);","+}","+","+inline constexpr SectionId model_id{runtime::hsm::any_device_id, runtime::hsm::model_id_tag};","+inline constexpr SectionId runtime_requirements{runtime::hsm::any_device_id, runtime::hsm::runtime_requirements_tag};","+inline constexpr SectionId model_struct{device_id, runtime::hsm::model_tag};","+inline constexpr SectionId weights{device_id, runtime::hsm::weights_tag};","+inline constexpr SectionId compiled_options{device_id, runtime::hsm::compiled_options_tag};","+// TEMPLATE-specific: layout version and feature flags, no common equivalent.","+inline constexpr SectionId blob_info{device_id, runtime::hsm::SectionTag::make_device_tag(3, /*is_inline=*/true)};","+","+/// Inline section: layout version of this plugin's own sections plus feature flags.","+struct BlobInfo {","+    static constexpr uint32_t current_layout_version = 1;","+    static constexpr uint32_t weights_embedded = 1u << 0;","+    static constexpr uint32_t weightless = 1u << 1;  //!< Model needs no weights at all - not just \"stored externally\".","+","+    uint32_t layout_version = current_layout_version;","+    uint32_t flags = 0;","+};","+static_assert(sizeof(BlobInfo) == 8, \"BlobInfo must fit the inline slot without padding\");","+","+}  // namespace hsm","+}  // namespace ov::template_plugin"],"additions":54,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/plugins/template/src/hsm_reader_handler.cpp","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@","+// Copyright (C) 2018-2026 Intel Corporation","+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+//","+","+#include \"hsm_reader_handler.hpp\"","+","+#include <algorithm>","+#include <string_view>","+","+#include \"openvino/core/except.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_model_id_codec.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/shared_buffer.hpp\"","+","+namespace ov::template_plugin {","+","+namespace {","+std::optional<std::string> decode_string(const runtime::hsm::Section& section) {","+    std::string value(section.size(), '\\0');","+    return section.read(value.data()) ? std::optional(std::move(value)) : std::nullopt;","+}","+","+std::optional<hsm::BlobInfo> decode_blob_info(const runtime::hsm::Section& section) {","+    hsm::BlobInfo info{};","+    return section.size() >= sizeof(info) && section.read(0, sizeof(info), &info) ? std::optional(info) : std::nullopt;","+}","+","+// Zero-copy only when the section's bytes are addressable AND something keeps them alive past this call","+// (m_source_blob) - a stream-backed import has neither, so it always copies into an owned buffer.","+std::shared_ptr<ov::AlignedBuffer> decode_buffer(const HsmReaderHandler& handler,","+                                                 const runtime::hsm::Section& section) {","+    const auto section_view = section.view();","+    if (handler.m_source_blob && !section_view.empty()) {","+        return std::make_shared<ov::SharedBuffer<std::shared_ptr<ov::AlignedBuffer>>>(","+            const_cast<std::byte*>(section_view.data()),","+            section_view.size(),","+            handler.m_source_blob);","+    } else {","+        auto buffer = std::make_shared<ov::AlignedBuffer>(section.size());","+        return section.read(buffer->get_ptr()) ? buffer : nullptr;","+    }","+}","+","+// Inverse of encode_compiled_options() in hsm_writer_handler.cpp - one `key=value` per line, split on the first '='.","+ov::AnyMap decode_compiled_options(std::string_view encoded) {","+    ov::AnyMap options;","+    while (!encoded.empty()) {","+        const auto line_end = std::min(encoded.find('\\n'), encoded.size());","+        const auto line = encoded.substr(0, line_end);","+        if (const auto separator = line.find('='); separator != std::string_view::npos) {","+            options.emplace(std::string(line.substr(0, separator)), std::string(line.substr(separator + 1)));","+        }","+        encoded.remove_prefix(std::min(line_end + 1, encoded.size()));","+    }","+    return options;","+}","+","+void set_model_id(HsmReaderHandler& handler, const runtime::hsm::Section& section) {","+    handler.m_model_id = runtime::hsm::decode_model_id(section);","+}","+","+void set_runtime_requirements(HsmReaderHandler& handler, const runtime::hsm::Section& section) {","+    handler.m_runtime_requirements = decode_string(section);","+}","+","+void set_model(HsmReaderHandler& handler, const runtime::hsm::Section& section) {","+    handler.m_model = decode_buffer(handler, section);","+}","+","+void set_weights(HsmReaderHandler& handler, const runtime::hsm::Section& section) {","+    // An empty section means \"no weights embedded\" (weightless) - a null buffer represents that, matching","+    // check_mandatory_sections()/read_hsm_blob()'s \"falsy means absent\" convention.","+    handler.m_weights = section.size() == 0 ? nullptr : decode_buffer(handler, section);","+}","+","+void set_compiled_options(HsmReaderHandler& handler, const runtime::hsm::Section& section) {","+    handler.m_compiled_options = decode_compiled_options(decode_string(section).value_or(\"\"));","+}","+","+void set_blob_info(HsmReaderHandler& handler, const runtime::hsm::Section& section) {","+    handler.m_blob_info = decode_blob_info(section);","+}","+}  // namespace","+","+const std::map<uint32_t, HsmReaderHandler::Decoder> HsmReaderHandler::s_decoders = {","+    // model id and weights are each registered under BOTH device scopes - a blob may carry either as a","+    // common (any_device_id) tag or scoped to this device, decoded identically either way.","+    {hsm::section_key(runtime::hsm::any_device_id, hsm::weights.tag), set_weights},","+    {hsm::section_key(hsm::model_id), set_model_id},","+    {hsm::section_key(hsm::device_id, hsm::model_id.tag), set_model_id},","+    {hsm::section_key(hsm::runtime_requirements), set_runtime_requirements},","+    {hsm::section_key(hsm::model_struct), set_model},","+    {hsm::section_key(hsm::weights), set_weights},","+    {hsm::section_key(hsm::compiled_options), set_compiled_options},","+    {hsm::section_key(hsm::blob_info), set_blob_info},","+};","+","+bool HsmReaderHandler::handle_section(const runtime::hsm::ManifestEntry& entry, const runtime::hsm::Section& section) {","+    if (const auto decoder = s_decoders.find(hsm::section_key(entry.device, entry.tag)); decoder != s_decoders.end()) {","+        decoder->second(*this, section);","+        return true;","+    } else {","+        return false;  // unrecognized (device, tag) pair - skip, per the unknown-tag rule.","+    }","+}","+","+void HsmReaderHandler::check_mandatory_sections() const {","+    OPENVINO_ASSERT(m_blob_info && m_blob_info->layout_version <= hsm::BlobInfo::current_layout_version,","+                    \"TEMPLATE: missing or unsupported blob info section\");","+    OPENVINO_ASSERT(m_model, \"TEMPLATE: missing mandatory model struct section\");","+}","+","+}  // namespace ov::template_plugin"],"additions":112,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/plugins/template/src/hsm_reader_handler.hpp","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@","+// Copyright (C) 2018-2026 Intel Corporation","+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+//","+","+// Reader-side HSM logic for this plugin: HsmReaderHandler is the ISectionReaderHandler that claims every","+// section of this blob (Core-owned and TEMPLATE-owned alike) during","+// ov::runtime::hsm::Reader::read_sections() dispatch - decoding is entirely internal to it, nothing is","+// exposed as a free function.","+","+#pragma once","+","+#include <map>","+#include <optional>","+#include <string>","+","+#include \"hsm_common.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/core/any.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/aligned_buffer.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/hsm_reader.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/tensor.hpp\"","+","+namespace ov::template_plugin {","+","+class HsmReaderHandler final : public runtime::hsm::ISectionReaderHandler {","+public:","+    bool handle_section(const runtime::hsm::ManifestEntry& entry, const runtime::hsm::Section& section) override;","+","+    void check_mandatory_sections() const;","+","+    std::shared_ptr<ov::AlignedBuffer> m_source_blob;  // Set before read_sections() when importing ov::Tensor","+    std::optional<uint64_t> m_model_id;","+    std::optional<std::string> m_runtime_requirements;","+    std::shared_ptr<ov::AlignedBuffer> m_model;","+    std::shared_ptr<ov::AlignedBuffer> m_weights;","+    std::optional<hsm::BlobInfo> m_blob_info;","+    ov::AnyMap m_compiled_options;","+","+private:","+    using Decoder = void (*)(HsmReaderHandler&, const runtime::hsm::Section&);","+    static const std::map<uint32_t, Decoder> s_decoders;","+};","+","+}  // namespace ov::template_plugin"],"additions":43,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/plugins/template/src/hsm_writer_handler.cpp","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,271 @@","+// Copyright (C) 2018-2026 Intel Corporation","+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+//","+","+#include \"hsm_writer_handler.hpp\"","+","+#include <functional>","+#include <optional>","+#include <ostream>","+#include <streambuf>","+#include <string>","+#include <string_view>","+#include <type_traits>","+","+#include \"openvino/core/except.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/pass/serialize.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/compilation_context.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/runtime/properties.hpp\"","+#include \"openvino/util/hash_util.hpp\"","+","+namespace ov::template_plugin {","+","+namespace {","+// Page-aligned start keeps the large sections mmap/DMA friendly; no slot padding, nothing follows that needs it.","+constexpr runtime::hsm::SectionAlignment page_alignment{util::min_page_alignment, 0};","+","+// Forwards written chunks to a sink (may be empty) and tracks the position for tellp(); never stores data.","+class ForwardingStreamBuf final : public std::streambuf {","+public:","+    using Callback = runtime::hsm::SectionSink;","+","+    explicit ForwardingStreamBuf(Callback callback = {}) : m_callback(std::move(callback)), m_pos(0) {}","+","+    size_t size() const noexcept {","+        return static_cast<size_t>(m_pos);","+    }","+","+protected:","+    std::streamsize xsputn(const char* s, std::streamsize n) override {","+        put(s, static_cast<size_t>(n));","+        return n;","+    }","+","+    int_type overflow(int_type ch) override {","+        if (!traits_type::eq_int_type(ch, traits_type::eof())) {","+            const auto c = traits_type::to_char_type(ch);","+            put(&c, 1);","+        }","+        return traits_type::not_eof(ch);","+    }","+","+    pos_type seekoff(off_type off, std::ios_base::seekdir dir, std::ios_base::openmode) override {","+        return off == 0 && dir == std::ios_base::cur ? pos_type(m_pos) : pos_type(off_type(-1));","+    }","+","+private:","+    void put(const char* data, size_t size) {","+        if (m_callback) {","+            m_callback({reinterpret_cast<const std::byte*>(data), size});","+        }","+        m_pos += static_cast<off_type>(size);","+    }","+","+    Callback m_callback;","+    off_type m_pos;","+};","+","+struct ModelStats {","+    size_t weights_size = 0;","+    uint64_t hash = 0;  // of the serialized structure and the weights size, not the weight values","+};","+","+// Serializes into counting/hashing buffers only, so nothing of the model is kept in memory.","+ModelStats measure_model(const std::shared_ptr<ov::Model>& model) {","+    uint64_t hash = 0;","+    ForwardingStreamBuf xml_buf{[&hash](ov::util::MemoryView chunk) {","+        const std::string_view text{reinterpret_cast<const char*>(chunk.data()), chunk.size()};","+        hash = util::u64_hash_combine(hash, std::hash<std::string_view>{}(text));","+    }};","+    ForwardingStreamBuf bin_buf;","+    std::ostream xml(&xml_buf), bin(&bin_buf);","+    ov::pass::Serialize(xml, bin).run_on_model(model);","+    return {bin_buf.size(), util::u64_hash_combine(hash, bin_buf.size())};","+}","+","+// Serializes the model in one pass: write_weights() streams the weights as produced and keeps the small XML for","+// write_structure(), so calling them in that order avoids a second pass.","+class ModelSerializer {","+public:","+    explicit ModelSerializer(std::shared_ptr<ov::Model> model) : m_model(std::move(model)) {}","+","+    void write_weights(const runtime::hsm::SectionSink& sink) {","+        auto& xml = m_xml.emplace();","+        ForwardingStreamBuf xml_buf{[&xml](ov::util::MemoryView chunk) {","+            xml.append(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(chunk.data()), chunk.size());","+        }};","+        ForwardingStreamBuf bin_buf{sink};","+        std::ostream xml_out(&xml_buf), bin_out(&bin_buf);","+        ov::pass::Serialize(xml_out, bin_out).run_on_model(m_model);","+    }","+","+    // Runs its own pass when write_weights() was not called before.","+    void write_structure(const runtime::hsm::SectionSink& sink) {","+        if (m_xml) {","+            sink({reinterpret_cast<const std::byte*>(m_xml->data()), m_xml->size()});","+            m_xml.reset();","+        } else {","+            ForwardingStreamBuf xml_buf{sink}, discard_buf;","+            std::ostream xml_out(&xml_buf), bin_out(&discard_buf);","+            ov::pass::Serialize(xml_out, bin_out).run_on_model(m_model);","+        }","+    }","+","+private:","+    std::shared_ptr<ov::Model> m_model;","+    std::optional<std::string> m_xml;","+};","+","+class SerializeEncoder final : public runtime::hsm::ISectionEncoder {","+public:","+    using Write = void (ModelSerializer::*)(const runtime::hsm::SectionSink&);","+","+    SerializeEncoder(std::shared_ptr<ModelSerializer> serializer, Write write)","+        : m_serializer(std::move(serializer)),","+          m_write(write) {}","+","+    void encode(const runtime::hsm::SectionSink& sink) const override {","+        ((*m_serializer).*m_write)(sink);","+    }","+","+private:","+    std::shared_ptr<ModelSerializer> m_serializer;","+    Write m_write;","+};","+","+// Cache-relevant options plus the weights path, which a weightless blob needs on import; restored through","+// Configuration.","+ov::AnyMap get_compiled_options(const Configuration& cfg, ov::AnyMap cache_options) {","+    if (!cfg.weights_path.empty()) {","+        cache_options.emplace(ov::weights_path.name(), cfg.weights_path.string());","+    }","+    return cache_options;","+}","+","+// One `key=value` per line; inverse of decode_compiled_options() in hsm_reader_handler.cpp.","+std::string encode_compiled_options(const ov::AnyMap& options) {","+    std::string encoded;","+    for (const auto& [key, value] : options) {","+        encoded.append(key).append(1, '=').append(value.as<std::string>()).append(1, '\\n');","+    }","+    return encoded;","+}","+}  // namespace","+","+/// Owns a small section's bytes (metadata only); large payloads must be streamed to avoid a second in-memory copy.","+class HsmWriterHandler::BytesEncoder final : public runtime::hsm::ISectionEncoder {","+    static constexpr auto max_size = util::min_page_alignment;  // one page","+public:","+    explicit BytesEncoder(std::string bytes) : m_bytes(std::move(bytes)) {","+        OPENVINO_ASSERT(m_bytes.size() <= max_size, \"TEMPLATE: HSM section too large to buffer: \", m_bytes.size());","+    }","+","+    template <class T>","+    static std::shared_ptr<BytesEncoder> from_value(const T& value) {","+        static_assert(std::is_trivially_copyable_v<T>);","+        return std::make_shared<BytesEncoder>(std::string(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&value), sizeof(T)));","+    }","+","+    size_t size() const noexcept {","+        return m_bytes.size();","+    }","+","+    ov::util::MemoryView view() const noexcept {","+        return {reinterpret_cast<const std::byte*>(m_bytes.data()), m_bytes.size()};","+    }","+","+    void encode(const runtime::hsm::SectionSink& sink) const override {","+        sink(view());","+    }","+","+private:","+    std::string m_bytes;","+};","+","+HsmWriterHandler::HsmWriterHandler(const std::shared_ptr<ov::Model>& model,"],"additions":185,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":496,"deletions":23,"truncated":true,"file_count":15},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-10-29T15:21:11.709988+00:00"}